StreamDevice
------------
The databases in Db/ that talk to libcom1 devices (read_all_array, com1_get, the acknowledged
sets, identity and streaming in Db/libcom1.proto) use plain %g numbers and work with an
unmodified StreamDevice.

Only the legacy single query (com1_getLink, "q01...") needs the custom %z format. If you use
it, add StreamDevice.LibCom1ExponentConverter.cc when installing the StreamDevice support
module for EPICS (see file for specifics). No database in this repository uses it.

Serial or TCP
-------------
The protocol file is the same for both, only the asyn port in st.cmd differs:

  drvAsynSerialPortConfigure("AVR11","COM11")            # USB serial
  drvAsynIPPortConfigure("OPTA1","192.168.1.50:5025")    # TCP, see AVR/libcom1/examples/EthernetExample

Alarms
------
The element records (e.g. $(DEVICE):i1:get_interlock) read the array record $(DEVICE):data
through CA links with MS, so they turn INVALID when the device stops answering. Keep the MS
when adding records, otherwise a dead device looks like a healthy one showing its last values.

Db/libcom1_device.db adds identity records (device name, firmware, channel order) for any
libcom1 device with protocol 2 firmware.
